# Grouping standing terms

Owner glossary for sorter / locks chats. Persist new locks same turn into `docs/order-grouping-sorter/order-grouping-locks.md` (hook stays in `supervisor-chat.mdc`). Detail / history: `docs/order-grouping-sorter/order-grouping-locks.md`. Run behaviour: `grouping.mdc`. Catalog fill policy (Supply Method, Printing Type, Supplier Name, Areeb): `.cursor/rules/custom-label-database/` — not duplicated here.

- **today** (ship-by) = run date **or overdue**, **or blank ship-by** (treat as today — if in ShipStation `awaiting_shipment`, pull today; locked 2026-09-24). Unparseable **non-blank** ship-by → unmatched. **Skip store `DTFOcean.co.uk WP`**. **Skip tag `00000-Warehouse OOS`** (locked 2026-10-09). **Skip tag `1006- PERSONALISED ORDER Listing Error (DW)`** (locked 2026-10-14). **Future ship-by** is written on **1st and 2nd** shift. **3rd shift and later** write overdue, blank, and the run-day ship-by. A later ship-by stays in `awaiting_shipment` unless the order has tag `1004- Personalised Design-Ready-` (locked 2026-10-14; ready-tag exception 2026-10-21; run day written 2026-10-22). **Hashim #037:** Shift 1 **order** volume **above 300** → leftover CSVs split today vs later; ≤300 → leftover may mix. **Fixed batches:** always one CSV per code per shift (today and later together on 1st/2nd; locked 2026-10-08). Do not dump overflow into Shift 2/3 as caps. Filename has **no** today/future slot.
- **order pool** = ShipStation `awaiting_shipment` **only**. No supervisor CSV/file (export has no tags).
- **batch** = one output CSV / pile (filename stem). Fixed: `B80` / `B100` / …; leftover Graph: `B1`, `B2`, … (skip reserved). Packing PIN: `{B}-S{n}-{process_number} Item {item_number}` (batch+shift only from filename). Leftover criteria: `Logs/Order Grouping Sorter/leftover_batches/{YYYY-MM-DD}.csv`.
- **fixed batch** = locked `B` code: **`B10` / `B40` / `B50` / `B70` / `B80` / `B90` / `B100` / `B1000` / `B1050` / `B1080` / `B2300` / `B2350` / `B2400` / `B3000` / `B3100` / `B3150` / `B3500` / `B3600` / `B3650` / `B3700` / `B3750` / `B4000` / `B4050` / `B5000` / `B5080` / `B5500` / `B6000` / `B6010` / `B6020` / `B6030` / `B6050` / `B6060` / `B700` / `B7000` / `B8000` / `B8050` / `B9000` / `B9040` / `B9050` / `B9100` / `B9150` / `B9200`** (shift is only `S{n}`). Row order in `fixed_batches.csv` = priority (first match wins; locked 2026-09-28). **B10** = ship-to country is filled in and is not `GB`. The row sits under the resend rows and above every product batch (locked 2026-10-21). An abroad resend stays in the resend rows. A blank country stays with the UK batches. **B6000** = UK plain and any line Item SKU contains `BG-Chinabag`. **B6010** = UK plain and any line Item SKU contains `BG125` (locked 2026-10-18). **B6020** = UK printed ready-made and any line Item SKU contains `BG-Chinabag`. **B6030** = UK printed ready-made and `BG125`. **B6050** = UK printed personalised and `BG-Chinabag`. **B6060** = UK printed personalised and `BG125` (locked 2026-10-21). **B700** = UK catalog Printing Type UV, under B10 and above Dancing Queen (locked 2026-10-20; an abroad UV order is B10 as of 2026-10-21). A UV resend stays in the resend rows. Plain orders do not enter B700. **B100** = own ready-made FOTL short-sleeve **Warehouse Stock**; **B50** = same as B100 but **Supplier On Demand** (locked 2026-09-30; B50 only). **B8000** / **B8050** = prime Fruit of the Loom ready-made / personalised, warehouse or on demand. Gildan stays **B40**. **Plain batch** leftover: `B2000`, `B2100`, `B2200`, `B2500`, `B2600`, `B2700`, … in order made.
- **process number** = increment inside a batch (`-1`, `-2`, …). Colour 3+ groups first, then **50 units** per process number. Same customer order stays on one process number. Not a new batch file.
- **item number** = `Item {n}` (space, not hyphen) — line inside that process number.
- **shift** = Packing Input folder + filename field 1 (after optional fixed-batch prefix). **Nth `--run` of the day = nth shift** (`SHIFT_PER_RUN`, locked 2026-10-14): 1st run → `1st Shift` / `S1`, 2nd → `2nd Shift` / `S2`, and so on. The pool is current `awaiting_shipment` only; an earlier shift CSV does not skip an order that is still awaiting (locked 2026-10-14). **3rd shift and later:** overdue, blank, and the run-day ship-by, plus tag `1004- Personalised Design-Ready-` when ship-by is later (locked 2026-10-22). A later ship-by without that tag stays out. No 300/100/100 write caps. `RESEND` / `UNMATCHED` have no shift slot; land in **this run’s** folder.
- **shift tag** (ShipStation, exact): `001-1st Shift`, `002-2nd Shift`, `003-3rd Shift`, `004-4th Shift`, `005-5th Shift`. Use these when the supervisor says our 1st–5th shift tag. Sorter intake still ignores them when choosing the folder. Locked 2026-10-14. **put the shift tag on these files** runs `scripts/tag_shift_orders.py` immediately (skips orders that already have it; parallel addtag). Locked 2026-10-18; parallel 2026-10-20.
- **add unmatched** = `scripts/seed_catalog_misses.py` only. Locked 2026-10-20.
- **Packs colour** = **later**. Do not guess Item 1 Colour. Do not dump mixed packs to unmatched. Packs still split on Areeb + Brand Name + Pack Size.
- **Fawad** = process-name slot for ShipStation store **MAS Clothing**. Amazon is **not** its own channel (`own`).
- **Definite match:** never guess. No definite match → **`UNMATCHED`**. Same customer order stays together.
- **Mixed P vs R** = majority printed **units**; **even → readymade**. Whole order together. Not unmatched. Locked 2026-09-17.
- **Personalised ready** = customised (P) piles only with tag **`1004- Personalised Design-Ready-`** (exact). Without → held this run. Readymade / plain unaffected. Locked 2026-09-25.
- **Item name Custom** = whole words **Custom**, **Customisable**, and **Customised** (personalised check and fixed-batch name contains). `Cause`, `customer`, and `customisation` do not count. `Personali` stays a substring. Locked 2026-10-14.
- **Mixed supply-method** = whole order **Supplier On Demand**. Not unmatched. Locked 2026-09-22.
- **Resend** = tag **`1014-ALL-RESEND` only** (not 1015/1016/1017). Fixed batches, first match: **B9000** ready-made and plain tees (not Gildan), **B9050** other personalised tees, **B9040** Gildan tees, **B9100** ready-made iron-on, **B9150** personalised iron-on, **B9200** any other resend. Catalog-miss resends stay `RESEND.csv`. Resend is not held for a missing `1004` tag. Locked 2026-10-18.
- **display** (Grouping Data Usage) = print that field on the **packing PDF** for that order’s page. Does not turn grouping off.
- Plain process files are also **stock-ordering piles**. Packs vs Gildan T-shirts = **30-chain** (product type / brand), not package-type.
- Graph values are **examples**, not a closed list — **except** Hashim #038 pick-list (`taxonomy_picklists.csv` / `taxonomy-picklist.mdc`).
- **In-house manufacturer** = iron-on or sticker in warehouse. **Plain cannot be in-house** → unmatched.
- Finish / SKU keys / printed-wins / attribute source: `grouping.mdc` (sorter stricter keys than universal `resolve_label`).
- **Order Grouping Sorter** = reads `awaiting_shipment` + three catalogs; writes one CSV per process into Packing Input. CLI default dry-run; `--run` writes. Testing: **`1st Shift`** every `--run`.
- **run the group sorter** / **group my awaiting shipment** / **run the sorter** = straight `--run` on current `awaiting_shipment`. No unmatched seed. No skip because an earlier shift CSV already has the order. If the shift was not named, ask which shift and do not run yet. Every chat and every new session. Locked 2026-10-14; catalog step removed 2026-10-20. Detail: `approval.mdc`.
